{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JfDC6fhg9UkdA7cByX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft it, a few questions. Your answers would change what the letter says:\n\n1. **Is there an open senior paralegal position, or would you be asking the firm to create one?** If there's a vacancy, the letter asks to be considered for it. If there isn't, it has to explain why the group needs a supervisor now, and the fact that you've trained all three new hires does most of that work.\n2. **Does the managing partner already know about the March deadline error?** I'd plan to mention it briefly and focus on the second-person check you added afterward. That shows the judgment a supervisor needs. If they know about it, leaving it out could look like you're hiding it. If they don't, you may still want it in, but that's your call.\n3. **Will any of the 4 lawyers you support back the request, and can I name them?** One line saying \"[Name] supports this\" carries a lot of weight with a managing partner.\n4. **Do you have any results to point to beyond the numbers above?** For example, deadlines the tracking sheet caught, time it saved, what you did on the 2 trials, or how quickly the new paralegals got up to speed.\n5. **What should the letter ask for, and what are the basics?** For example, a meeting, a decision by the next review cycle, or both. Also: is it an email or a formal letter, and what names should I use for you and the partner?\n\nIf you don't know some of these, just say so. I'll write around the gaps and won't guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":9551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics